\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  O world, thy life is ended
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 High on the cross suspended,
\par Today the saviour died.
\par The Lord of all creation
\par In shame and degradation
\par Was  scourged, reviled and crucified.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O saviour mine, who dareth
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To smite thee thus? who beareth
\par The guilt of Thy deep pain?
\par All here must make confession
\par Fulfilling thy commission,
\par The burdened world to save and free
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I make this sad confession
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 My sin and my transgression,
\par I know have stricken thee.
\par \pard\li135\sl190\slmult0  Now thou must bear affliction,
\par   Thy filling thy commission
\par \pard   The burdened world to save and free
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\cf0  The sorrows thou art bearing,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With none their burden sharing,
\par On me they ought to fall.
\par The torture thou art feeling,
\par Thy patient love revealing;
\par  'Tis I that should endure it all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy cross I would be sharing,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Whilst mine with patience bearing.
\par O'er coming evil lust
\par What Thy eyes do not favour,
\par I will forsake, dear saviour
\par My soul, my life, to Thee entrust.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

